WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.026
Two Sum asks which two numbers add to 9.

00:05.026 --> 00:12.690
Trying every pair means each number meets every other number.

00:12.690 --> 00:14.700
That is n² work.

00:15.000 --> 00:24.013
Instead, walk the list once and keep a map of numbers you have seen.

00:24.013 --> 00:31.700
Each entry remembers a number and the index where it sits.

00:32.000 --> 00:38.252
For each number, ask the map for its partner.

00:38.252 --> 00:47.700
9 minus 7 is 2, and 2 is already in the map, so the pair is 0 and 1.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.703
One pass, one map lookup each: O(n) time.

00:52.703 --> 00:59.700
That’s arrays and hashing: memory traded for instant lookups.

